Description: Export the icons of menu items with the menus which Firefox exports over D-Bus.
 Items of the History and Bookmarks menus show the icon of their page in the menus in the window, but the global
 menu bar (widget.gtk.global-menu.enabled) exported them without icons, as a TODO in the code noted. Each exported
 item now loads the icon which NativeMenu::GetIcon() finds for it with IconLoader, as Firefox's own macOS menu bar
 does (nsMenuItemIconX), and sets it as the item's icon-data once it is loaded, as a PNG of 32x32 pixels, twice the
 size at which menus show icons, so that they stay sharp on screens with a scale of up to 2. A vector icon is drawn
 with the context paint of the item's style, as on macOS. A menu item adds its icon, an <img> child, only when it is
 first shown, after the item was exported. NativeMenu::GetIconOwner() recognizes such an image, and the model is
 dirtied when one is added or removed or its src or srcset changes, so that the icons of the items are looked at
 again when the model is recomputed. NativeMenu::GetIcon() flushes style, which must not happen while the DOM is
 being changed, so the menu bar's model is recomputed from a runnable, which handles all the changes of a task at
 once, like the icons which a menu adds to all its items when it is shown, while the models of native context menus
 are recomputed right away as before. An item loads its icon again only when the icon's URL changes.
 .
 The desktop shows the icons as they are drawn, and its menus can have another color scheme than Firefox's, like
 dark menus in the top bar and light windows. The new preference widget.gtk.global-menu.icon-color-scheme sets the
 color scheme of the desktop's menus: 0 dark, 1 light, and 2, the default, the color scheme and text color of
 Firefox's own menus. With dark or light, a vector icon is drawn in that color scheme, so that an SVG favicon with a
 variant for the dark color scheme draws the matching one, and its context paint has the text color of Firefox's
 menus in that color scheme (MenuText) where it has the text color of the menu item, so that the icon of a page
 without a favicon matches the labels. SVGImageContext::MaybeStoreContextPaint() accepts the color scheme and the
 value of currentcolor for that. Icons are loaded again when the preference changes.
